    "code_current_through_note": "eCode360 breadcrumb shows 'Code 2025-03-19'. Newest codified zoning ordinance seen: Ord. No. 2024-04 (9-18-2024) in 270-5.2. New Laws: Ord. No. 2026-02 (2026-11-04, Zoning Amendment), not codified.",
    "code_caution": "A zoning amendment, Ord. No. 2026-02, was adopted on 2026-11-04 and is not yet in the online code. It was not read, so it may change these rules. Ask the Township.",
    "checks": [
      "An ADU is a permitted accessory use (zoning permit) in the A, RB, RL, RM, VR, VC, CBC, AH, RCC and E zones, with a single-family detached house or a twin half (270-2.2, zone use lists B(5))",
      "Family only: the unit is 'for immediate family of the principal building occupants, including parents, grandparents, children, and grandchildren'. It may not be a dwelling for anyone outside the family, and the owners must record a notarized covenant saying so before the permit (270-2.2, 270-5.2A(11), (12))",
      "The landowner must live in the house or the ADU. All occupants of both units together may not exceed the definition of family (270-5.2A(6), (7))",
      "At most 40% of the total square footage of the house. One ADU per lot. Architecturally consistent with the house (270-5.2A(3), (4), (8))",
      "The ADU meets the zone's setbacks, height, coverage, lot width and every other single-family detached dimensional rule (270-5.2A(1), (5)). Each zone table has its own 'Accessory Dwelling' setback column. In A, VR, VC and E it may not stand in the front yard",
      "One parking space more than the house needs (270-5.2A(10))",
      "On-lot sewage rules apply where there is no public sewer (270-5.2A(2)). The A zone has no public sewer or water",
      "The ADU meets the zone's setbacks, height, coverage and lot width (270-5.2A(1)) and every other single-family detached dimensional rule (A(5)). 270-5.2A does not say whether zone densities (RL three, RM four, AH one, RCC eight units per acre) or the VR and VC lot area per unit count the ADU as a dwelling unit. Ask the zoning officer",
      "In the E zone a house is allowed only with a horticultural operation (270-3.12B(1)(c)), so an ADU there needs that house",
      "Historic conversions (270-5.2FF) are a separate use, special exception in A and by right in AH, for historic structures. Whether they can add a dwelling was not settled",
      "A two-family conversion of an existing single-family detached house is a separate use: by right in A, RB, VR, VC and CBC, special exception in RM. No change to the outside of the building except for safety (270-2.2, 270-5.2III)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: East Hempfield Township (easthempfield.org). Read on eCode360 in a browser, one section print view at a time. The term is 'accessory dwelling' in 270-2.2 and 'accessory dwelling units' in the zone lists and 270-5.2A. Use lists read for every zone except TR. The C, ME and ROS lists do not name ADUs. Second reading on 2026-11-26 in a browser on eCode360: 270-5.2A (A(1) names setbacks, height, coverage and lot width, not density; the check was reworded), 270-5.2FF and the 270-2.2 'historic conversion' definition ('The adaptation of a historic structure into a new appropriate use'). Ord. No. 2026-02 (PDF) still not read."
